.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-4.txt:18:1. **SEVERITY: P1 annex — mandatory cure before GA**  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-4.txt:20:   **Concrete failure scenario:** These diff-added canonical comments call work “cheap,” assert that operations take “seconds,” and claim “nothing” or “zero marginal cost.” That violates the explicit no-speed-claim rule at `AGENTS.md:9-11`. It is the same P1 class already recognized by conditions 19 and 24, but these workflow lines are not declared there. Release evidence would therefore claim compliance while shipping positive performance assertions that can become false as runners or workloads change.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-4.txt:23:### P2 follow-ups
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/verdict-rc1-4.txt:25:1. **SEVERITY: P2 follow-up**  
