.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga/verdict-ga-3.txt:19:- P2 — `scripts/uninstall.sh:15,522,526-547,318-349` — The help and dry-run still describe a `.claude/`-only backup/restore, but the added implementation archives and may restore every valid manifest-listed delivery outside `.claude/`. An adopter expecting a governance-only restore can have absent `docs/`, `.github/`, `SPEC/` or root deliveries recreated without that scope appearing in the preview. Minimal fix: describe the complete archive scope in `--help` and print the affected member set during dry-run.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga/verdict-ga-3.txt:21:- P2 — `templates/.github/workflows/validate.yml.template:124-128` — Once activated, the workflow installs a floating `PyYAML>=6.0,<7` package and imports it in the CI job. A subsequently compromised or behavior-changing 6.x release therefore executes in adopter CI despite the same workflow emphasizing immutable pins elsewhere. Minimal fix: install from an exact, hash-locked dependency set or use a pinned, vendored validator.
